summary:
  This daily radiology news briefing highlights recent advancements and important updates relevant to senior residents. Key topics include emerging research on metabolic health and diabetes, potential risks associated with seemingly safer alternatives, and insights into chronic conditions like heart health. 
  Several articles address new discoveries with implications for clinical practice and patient management, offering valuable content for board preparation and staying current in the field.

top_stories[8]{title,source,url,category,importance,ai_summary}:
  Title: Spikes in blood sugar after eating may be more dangerous for the brain than previously thought.
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/01/260114084134.htm
  category: research
  importance: 95
  ai_summary: "A massive genetic study reveals a higher risk of Alzheimer’s disease in individuals with elevated post-meal blood sugar, suggesting hidden biological pathways are involved."
  Title: Northwestern Medicine’s new antibody wakes the immune system against pancreatic cancer
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/01/260114084129.htm
  category: research
  importance: 90
  ai_summary: "Researchers developed an antibody that targets a protective signal on pancreatic cancer cells, leading to immune system activation and slowed tumor growth in animal models."
  Title: Scientists uncover a hidden type of diabetes in newborns
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/01/260114084125.htm
  category: research
  importance: 85
  ai_summary: "A newly discovered rare diabetes in newborns is caused by a single gene mutation affecting insulin production, often presenting with neurological complications."
  Title: Scientists finally uncover why statins cause muscle pain
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/01/260114084122.htm
  category: research
  importance: 80
  ai_summary: "Research indicates that statins can cause muscle pain by triggering a calcium leak within muscle cells, providing a biological explanation for a common side effect."
  Title: Scientists question the safety of BPA-free packaging
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/01/260114084134.htm
  category: research
  importance: 75
  ai_summary: "A McGill University study suggests that BPA substitutes in food packaging may pose health risks by interfering with ovarian cell function and potentially having similar effects to BPA."
